        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenny Greene, Billy Idol, Dave Hall, Mary J. Blige\n- Groups: Intro\n- Works: \"Love No Limit\", \"What's the 411?\"\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, musician, singer, songwriter, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Billy Idol was born as William Michael Albert Broad on 30 November 1955 and is an English musician, singer, songwriter, and actor.\n- Kenny Greene was born on January 17, 1969 and was an American singer-songwriter.\n- Kenny Greene was a member of the R&B group Intro.\n- \"Love No Limit\" was co-written by Kenny Greene and Dave Hall for Mary J. Blige's debut album \"What's the 411?\".\n- Kenny Greene died on October 1, 2001.",
